    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\sin\\theta=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt5},\\quad \\cos\\theta=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt5},\\quad \\tan\\theta=\\dfrac12.$\n\n$\\csc\\theta=\\sqrt5,\\quad \\sec\\theta=\\dfrac{\\sqrt5}{2},\\quad \\cot\\theta=2.$",
      "worked": "By Pythagoras, the hypotenuse is $h=\\sqrt{1^2+2^2}=\\sqrt5$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}=\\frac1{\\sqrt5}\\\\\n\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{hypotenuse}}=\\frac2{\\sqrt5}\\\\\n\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac12\\\\\n\\csc\\theta&=\\frac{\\text{hypotenuse}}{\\text{opposite}}=\\sqrt5\\\\\n\\sec\\theta&=\\frac{\\text{hypotenuse}}{\\text{adjacent}}=\\frac{\\sqrt5}{2}\\\\\n\\cot\\theta&=\\frac{\\text{adjacent}}{\\text{opposite}}=2.\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
